---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout title="Support | Forge & Field Supply"><section class="page-hero container"><p class="eyebrow">Keep gear useful</p><h1>Support</h1><p>Support content prioritizes care, repair, fit, and warranty decisions before pushing replacement.</p></section><section class="supportList container"><details open><summary>Sizing and fit</summary><p>Measure the body or existing gear first; use product dimensions instead of assuming a familiar size label transfers across equipment types.</p></details><details><summary>Repairs</summary><p>Field repairs are documented by material and failure type, with replacement hardware listed where practical.</p></details><details><summary>Returns</summary><p>The demo policy separates unused returns from warranty or repair requests so each path asks for the right evidence.</p></details><details><summary>Warranty</summary><p>Manufacturing defects and ordinary wear are evaluated differently; useful repair options remain visible in both cases.</p></details></section><section class="container"><form class="supportForm" id="support-form"><label>Email<input required type="email" autocomplete="email"></label><label>Topic<select><option>Fit / sizing</option><option>Repair</option><option>Return</option><option>Warranty</option></select></label><label>Question<textarea required rows="5"></textarea></label><button class="button" type="submit">Complete support demo</button><p class="status" id="support-status" role="status" hidden>Demo support request complete. Nothing was transmitted.</p></form></section><script>document.getElementById('support-form')?.addEventListener('submit',e=>{e.preventDefault();document.getElementById('support-status').hidden=false;});</script></SiteLayout>